# Application Frozen on Production

## Tags

* type: bug
* assigned:
* priority: high
* status: open
* keywords: gn-guile
* interested: alexk, bonfacem, fredm, pjotrp

## Description

gn-guile, will after a while, seemingly stop responding on the port that it listens on.

The container's `/var/log/gn-guile.log` file is empty.

When you go into the container and check status, it indicates it's still running, e.g.

```
$ herd status gn-guile -n 200
Status of gn-guile:
  It is running since Wed Oct  7 19:04:55 2026 (7 days ago).
  Main PID: 47
  Command: /gnu/store/a2zi4xi8xnv8kaka8ka2dv6wr5ci0kzn-gn-guile-pola-wrapper 127.0.0.1 8091
  It is enabled.
  Provides: gn-guile
  Requires: networking
  Will be respawned.
  Log file: /var/log/gn-guile.log

Recent messages:
  .
  .
  .
  2026-10-09 04:40:49 ;;; ("https://query.wikidata.org/sparql?query=SELECT%20DISTINCT%20%3Fstripped_alias%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20WHERE%20%7B%20%3Cstyle%3E%20rdfs%3Alabel%20%3Fname%20%3B%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20
%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20skos%3AaltLabel%20%3Falias%20.%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20BIND%20%28STR%28%3Falias%29%20%20AS%20%3Fstripped_alias%29%20.%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20
%20%20%20FILTER%28LANG%28%
  2026-10-09 04:40:49 3Fname%29%20%3D%20%22en%22%20%26%26%20LANG%28%3Falias%29%20%3D%20%22en%22%29.%7D")
  2026-10-09 04:40:49
  2026-10-09 04:40:49 ;;; ("* { margin: 0; padding: 0; }")
  .
  .
  .
```

but when you check with curl:

```
$ curl -X GET "http://localhost:8091"
curl: (28) Failed to connect to localhost port 8091 after 134008 ms: Could not connect to server
```

After restarting the application (`herd restart gn-guile`), the application starts responding normally.

```
$ curl -X GET "http://localhost:8091"
{"name":"GeneNetwork REST API","version":"4.0.0","comment":"This is the official REST API for the GeneNetwork service hosted at https://genenetwork.org/","license":{"source code (unless otherwise specified)":"Affero GNU Public License 3.0 (AGPL3)","data (unless otherwise specified)":"Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0)"},"note":"This is work in progress (WIP). Note that the final base URL will change! The temporary prefix is:","prefix":"http://localhost:8091","links":{"species":"http://localhost:8091/species.meta.json"}
```

My (fredm) current guess is that some error leads the gn-guile app to enter failure mode where it drops into the debugger. The app stops being responsive, but it is not technically dead. Thus, "herd" sees it as running, but any other service depending on the application runs into the timeout issue.


From the logs from "herd" we see that something is actually sending a gene-alias query of `"* { margin: 0; padding: 0; }"`. This implies that something that can access localhost is sending `/gene/aliases/* { margin: 0; padding: 0; }`.

After a little bit of digging, it looks like this might be one of:

=> genenetwork2/gn2/wqflask/search_results.py:        urljoin(GN_GUILE_SERVER_URL, f"gene/aliases/{symbol_string}"))
=> genenetwork2/gn2/base/trait.py:                                f"gene/aliases/{self.symbol.upper()}"),
=> genenetwork2/gn2/base/trait.py:                                f"gene/aliases/{self.symbol.capitalize()}"),
=> genenetwork2/gn2/base/trait.py:                                f"gene/aliases/{self.symbol.lower()}"))))

I tried reproducing the issue by doing a search, but that did not work.

For now, I simply added some extra logging to GN2 to try and surface the issue, see

=> https://github.com/genenetwork/genenetwork2/commit/d96ee76e15b6ee109e786bb82145a1574464af5d
